limine is a modern, minimal bootloader
upstream: https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine
license: BSD-2-Clause
ported to hdxp by: davy
 
builds the uefi x86-64 loader and installs it to /boot/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI.
requires your EFI System Partition mounted at /boot first.
you write /boot/limine.conf yourself, eg:
 
  timeout: 5
 
  /HDXI
      protocol: linux
      path: boot():/vmlinuz
      cmdline: root=PARTUUID=<your-root-partuuid> rw init=/sbin/init
 
